 "segments": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "s": 0.35,
   "e": 5.432,
   "text": "The dream of self-adapting neural networks is not a new idea.",
   "dur": 5.082,
   "voiced": 319,
   "sim": 0.86,
   "f0": 118.542,
   "st": -1.329,
   "range_st": 7.369,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "s": 5.652,
   "e": 10.644,
   "text": "In fact, it is historically older than backpropagation itself.",
   "dur": 4.992,
   "voiced": 250,
   "sim": 0.859,
   "f0": 126.703,
   "st": -0.176,
   "range_st": 7.757,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "s": 11.615,
   "e": 18.986,
   "text": "In 1949, Canadian psychologist Donald Hebb published The Organization of Behavior,",
   "dur": 7.371,
   "voiced": 435,
   "sim": 0.853,
   "f0": 134.232,
   "st": 0.823,
   "range_st": 8.206,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "s": 19.107,
   "e": 23.812,
   "text": "introducing his foundational postulate of synaptic plasticity:",
   "dur": 4.705,
   "voiced": 245,
   "sim": 0.851,
   "f0": 125.01,
   "st": -0.409,
   "range_st": 8.084,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "s": 24.022,
   "e": 29.219,
   "text": "when an axon of cell A is near enough to excite cell B",
   "dur": 5.197,
   "voiced": 304,
   "sim": 0.858,
   "f0": 120.685,
   "st": -1.019,
   "range_st": 4.277,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "s": 29.472,
   "e": 32.568,
   "text": "and repeatedly takes part in firing it,",
   "dur": 3.096,
   "voiced": 167,
   "sim": 0.864,
   "f0": 125.776,
   "st": -0.303,
   "range_st": 8.87,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "s": 33.144,
   "e": 37.529,
   "text": "some growth process or metabolic change takes place.",
   "dur": 4.385,
   "voiced": 231,
   "sim": 0.807,
   "f0": 123.644,
   "st": -0.599,
   "range_st": 5.175,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "s": 38.979,
   "e": 42.912,
   "text": "In popular culture, this became the famous adage:",
   "dur": 3.932,
   "voiced": 203,
   "sim": 0.856,
   "f0": 122.67,
   "st": -0.736,
   "range_st": 9.109,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 2,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "s": 43.264,
   "e": 47.336,
   "text": "neurons that fire together, wire together.",
   "dur": 4.072,
   "voiced": 238,
   "sim": 0.796,
   "f0": 119.931,
   "st": -1.127,
   "range_st": 8.705,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "s": 47.96,
   "e": 59.856,
   "text": "In the decades that followed, mathematical theorists attempted to transform Hebb's intuitive biological principle into rigorous computational learning algorithms.",
   "dur": 11.896,
   "voiced": 676,
   "sim": 0.883,
   "f0": 132.746,
   "st": 0.63,
   "range_st": 8.335,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 2,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "s": 60.935,
   "e": 68.882,
   "text": "In 1982, Finnish mathematician Erkki Oja introduced normalized Hebbian learning,",
   "dur": 7.948,
   "voiced": 459,
   "sim": 0.845,
   "f0": 138.206,
   "st": 1.328,
   "range_st": 9.281,
   "asr": 0.933,
   "attempts": 2,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "s": 69.21,
   "e": 80.776,
   "text": "proving that a single neuron equipped with local weight decay could mathematically discover the principal eigenvector of its input distribution",
   "dur": 11.566,
   "voiced": 616,
   "sim": 0.873,
   "f0": 124.916,
   "st": -0.422,
   "range_st": 7.268,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "s": 80.999,
   "e": 85.557,
   "text": "without any external teacher or global loss function.",
   "dur": 4.558,
   "voiced": 253,
   "sim": 0.823,
   "f0": 129.735,
   "st": 0.233,
   "range_st": 8.08,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "s": 86.311,
   "e": 91.45,
   "text": "Concurrently, Teuvo Kohonen invented Self-Organizing Maps,",
   "dur": 5.139,
   "voiced": 304,
   "sim": 0.888,
   "f0": 129.817,
   "st": 0.244,
   "range_st": 9.35,
   "asr": 0.857,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "s": 92.07,
   "e": 98.19,
   "text": "showing that uncoordinated, localized competition between neighboring units",
   "dur": 6.12,
   "voiced": 368,
   "sim": 0.882,
   "f0": 128.333,
   "st": 0.045,
   "range_st": 7.018,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "s": 98.494,
   "e": 107.381,
   "text": "could spontaneously fold a high-dimensional feature space into a beautifully ordered topological manifold.",
   "dur": 8.887,
   "voiced": 496,
   "sim": 0.871,
   "f0": 126.561,
   "st": -0.196,
   "range_st": 7.32,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "s": 108.081,
   "e": 115.047,
   "text": "Later, researchers expanded this with BCM theory and Dynamic Rewiring Networks,",
   "dur": 6.966,
   "voiced": 419,
   "sim": 0.861,
   "f0": 126.148,
   "st": -0.252,
   "range_st": 8.928,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "s": 115.238,
   "e": 126.57,
   "text": "adding structural plasticity rules where weak connections were pruned and new synaptic edges were randomly sprouted in response to local activity levels.",
   "dur": 11.332,
   "voiced": 635,
   "sim": 0.871,
   "f0": 128.589,
   "st": 0.079,
   "range_st": 7.236,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "s": 127.69,
   "e": 132.858,
   "text": "The self-organizing hypothesis was breathtakingly elegant:",
   "dur": 5.168,
   "voiced": 244,
   "sim": 0.872,
   "f0": 125.128,
   "st": -0.393,
   "range_st": 7.139,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 1,
   "level": 0
  },
  {
   "i": 19,
   "s": 133.036,
   "e": 138.901,
   "text": "if we simply give a network the freedom to sculpt its own wiring using local rules,",
   "dur": 5.865,
   "voiced": 379,
   "sim": 0.88,
   "f0": 126.619,
   "st": -0.188,
   "range_st": 8.163,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 20,
   "s": 139.042,
   "e": 148.095,
   "text": "general intelligence, modular specialization, and dynamic routing will organically emerge from the bottom up.",
   "dur": 9.052,
   "voiced": 535,
   "sim": 0.869,
   "f0": 127.14,
   "st": -0.117,
   "range_st": 7.633,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 21,
   "s": 148.795,
   "e": 153.999,
   "text": "For decades, this was viewed as the holy grail of artificial intelligence.",
   "dur": 5.204,
   "voiced": 299,
   "sim": 0.816,
   "f0": 121.598,
   "st": -0.888,
   "range_st": 9.77,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 22,
   "s": 154.691,
   "e": 164.404,
   "text": "It promised networks that could learn continuously without catastrophic forgetting, growing new modules dynamically as needed.",
   "dur": 9.713,
   "voiced": 536,
   "sim": 0.814,
   "f0": 126.522,
   "st": -0.201,
   "range_st": 7.268,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 23,
   "s": 165.104,
   "e": 170.87,
   "text": "Yet when these ideas were pushed to the scale of modern deep learning,",
   "dur": 5.766,
   "voiced": 343,
   "sim": 0.891,
   "f0": 119.395,
   "st": -1.205,
   "range_st": 6.893,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 24,
   "s": 171.264,
   "e": 173.236,
   "text": "an unexpected crisis emerged.",
   "dur": 1.972,
   "voiced": 92,
   "sim": 0.702,
   "f0": 128.868,
   "st": 0.117,
   "range_st": 8.9,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  },
  {
   "i": 25,
   "s": 173.456,
   "e": 180.9,
   "text": "The promised organic modularity failed to materialize, stalling in chaotic representational collapse.",
   "dur": 7.444,
   "voiced": 460,
   "sim": 0.755,
   "f0": 126.76,
   "st": -0.168,
   "range_st": 5.94,
   "asr": 1.0,
   "attempts": 0,
   "reused": true
  }
 ]
}